# TypeScript Strict Mode

## Principle
Enable strict TypeScript for safer code.

## Guidelines
- Set `"strict": true` in tsconfig.json
- Use explicit return types on public APIs
- Avoid `any`; prefer `unknown` with type guards
- Enable `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
- Use Astro's type definitions for frontmatter

## tsconfig.json
```json
{
  "extends": "astro/tsconfigs/strict",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strictNullChecks": true,
    "noImplicitAny": true
  }
}
```

## Benefits
Catch errors at compile time, better refactoring support.
